## Parameter selection (data-driven, whitened space)

- TSVD: GCV over k selected k = 26; discrepancy criterion (min |RSS(k) - (m-k)|) selected k = 25. Reported solution uses GCV.
- Tikhonov: GCV selected lambda = 0.699216 (effective dof 25.5); L-curve corner at lambda = 4.43217; discrepancy at lambda = 1.2452. Reported solution uses GCV.
- CGLS: Morozov discrepancy rule: stop at the first iteration with whitened residual <= sqrt(m - dof_ref) = 14.000 (dof_ref = 26 from the TSVD/GCV analysis); stopped at iteration 14 (residual 13.9918).

## Consistency across criteria

- Effective DOFs: TSVD 26, Tikhonov 25.5, CGLS ~26.
- Pairwise relative solution differences: TSVD vs Tikhonov 0.512, TSVD vs CGLS 0.630, Tikhonov vs CGLS 0.297.

## Judgment

- Discrepancy check: the whitened residual of every method sits at its target sqrt(m - dof) within 1.7% (deviations 1.7% / 1.6% / 0.1% for TSVD / Tikhonov / CGLS); differences of this size are within the statistical fluctuation of the residual norm (se ~ 5%), so no method over- or under-fits.
- Effective DOFs agree across methods: TSVD 26 (exact), Tikhonov 25.5 (filter factors), CGLS 26.2 (from E[RSS] = m - dof).
- Consensus view: relative solution differences TSVD-Tikhonov 0.512, TSVD-CGLS 0.630, Tikhonov-CGLS 0.297; the medoid (smallest total distance to the other two) is Tikhonov.
- Filter character: TSVD hard-truncates at k = 26 (ringing risk at the cutoff), Tikhonov damps all components smoothly, CGLS reaches an equivalently filtered solution after 14 iterations (early stopping acts as the regularization).
- **Recommended: Tikhonov** (parameter 0.699216): satisfies the discrepancy principle (whitened residual 13.7908 vs target 14.019, deviation 1.6%), its effective dof (25.5) matches the independent TSVD-GCV and CGLS estimates, it is the consensus (medoid) solution of the three strategies, and its smooth filter avoids hard-truncation artifacts. All parameters were selected from the data only (GCV / L-curve / discrepancy in whitened space; no access to the true x).
